 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This Thursday, you left again\nThe light of your face and always.\nIt will be our night no enough\nFor such an evening as yours because\nWe sleep where we shall sleep with forget\nThe morning's colour forever.\nI too will know the thing that was never,\nAnd all shall have it to ourselves. Ever\nThere must be something else but this today,\nA sore sorrow for that which has away,\nTo wake us one more time not here again,\nWith lips of knowledge, senses",
